---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../config/site'
import '../styles/doc.css'
---

<!-- Answers questions about the product; /support is where you write to a
     person. Keep the two from duplicating: no "email us" wall of text here. -->
<LegalLayout
  title={`FAQ — ${site.name}`}
  description={`Common questions about ${site.name}: Coins and Gems, AI opponents, difficulty tiers, board themes, offline play, and account questions.`}
  canonical={`${site.url}/faq`}
>
  <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <p class="doc-meta">
    Rules questions are answered on <a href="/rules">Backgammon Rules</a>.
    Anything not here, write to <a href="/support">Support</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Playing</h2>

  <h3>Is it free?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. You can play every tier, unlock boards, and climb the ranks without
    paying. Purchases are optional and buy Coins or Gems, never an advantage in
    the dice.
  </p>

  <h3>Am I playing a person or a computer?</h3>
  <p>
    Both happen. Matchmaking looks for a human first and pairs you with an AI
    opponent when nobody is free at your tier, so a game always starts.
    <a href="/fair-play">Fair Play</a> explains how the AI works.
  </p>

  <h3>How hard is the AI?</h3>
  <p>
    There are five difficulty tiers, from a gentle opponent for a first game up
    to one that punishes loose checkers. Higher tiers also play for higher
    stakes in Coins.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I play offline?</h3>
  <p>
    Matches against other players need a connection, because the dice come from
    our servers. A local match against the AI keeps working when the signal
    drops; your rewards and stats sync once you are back online.
  </p>

  <h3>What happens if I disconnect mid-match?</h3>
  <p>
    The match lives on the server, not on your phone, so a dropped signal does
    not wipe the board. Stay away too long and the match is forfeited to your
    opponent — see <a href="/community-rules">Community Rules</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Why can I not make that move?</h3>
  <p>
    Because it is not legal for that roll. The board highlights every move you
    are allowed to make, including the rule that forces you to use both dice
    when possible. The <a href="/rules">rules page</a> covers the awkward cases:
    the bar, blocked entry, and bearing off with a high die.
  </p>

  <h2>Coins, Gems, and the shop</h2>

  <h3>What is the difference between Coins and Gems?</h3>
  <p>
    Coins are the everyday currency you win and stake in matches. Gems are the
    rarer one, used for premium unlocks. Both are virtual: {site.disclaimer}
  </p>

  <h3>I ran out of Coins. Now what?</h3>
  <p>
    Wait for the hourly bonus, spin the wheel, or finish your daily missions.
    Coins come back for free; you never have to buy them.
  </p>

  <h3>I paid and nothing arrived.</h3>
  <p>
    Send us the store receipt and we will fix the balance. Refunds go through
    the App Store or Google Play, since that is who took the payment.
    <a href="/support">Support</a> has the details to include.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I cash out my Coins?</h3>
  <p>
    No. Coins and Gems have no cash value and cannot be sold, cashed out, or
    traded outside the app. See <a href="/responsible-play">Responsible Play</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>

  <h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
  <p>
    You can start playing straight away. Signing in links your progress to you,
    so a new phone does not mean a fresh start.
  </p>

  <h3>Will I lose my progress if I change phone?</h3>
  <p>
    Not if you have signed in. A guest account lives on the device only — sign
    in before you switch phones.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I change my display name?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes, from your profile. Names are public to opponents, so
    <a href="/community-rules">Community Rules</a> apply to them.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
  <p>
    Follow <a href="/delete-account">Delete Your Account</a>. Deletion is
    permanent and removes your profile, balances, and match history.
  </p>

  <h3>Which data do you hold?</h3>
  <p>
    The account, the profile, the balances, and the matches — the detail is in
    the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. We never see your card: payments
    stay with the app stores.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
